To learn the sparse representation of a certain word $w$,
we propose the following optimization objective
\begin{align}
   \min_{\vector x}\ \ & \| \vector{Ux} - \vector{w} \|_{2}^{2} + \alpha \|\vector{x}\|_1 +
   \beta |\trans{\vector{1}} \vector{x} - 1| \nonumber\\
   &{} + \gamma \trans{\vector{1}} \max \{\vector{0}, -\vector{x}\},  \label{eq:opt_sp}
\end{align}
where $\max$ denotes the component-wise maximum;  $\vector{w}$ is the embedding for a rare word $w\in \mathcal{C}$.

